Sonja Kisa wrote:

> Now how do i install the patches? I assume I put the diff file in the
> nethack folder, then what?

You have to compile your own version of the game to apply the patches. 
This might be hard or very easy, depending on whether you have done this 
kind of thing before.

If you feel up to it (and if you're not affraid of the command prompt 
and have a little computer knowledge, it isn't that hard) you have to 
download the source from www.nethack.org; if you unpack it, there is a 
file on how to compile it on your platform in the sys/winnt directory (I 
think this is also for compiling on Win98, but I'm not sure). I 
reccomend using MinGW as a compiler, since that worked for me.

First try to compile vanilla, and if that works, patch the source with 
the diff file (you'll need the patch program for this, which you can 
download; google for it) and compile it again. To get bones and save 
compatibility with the official windows version, you'll have to select 
the same options for your build (set in config.h) as in the official one 
(see the #version command in the game); I also had to set 'cflags = 
-mms-bitfields' in the makefile for it to work, but you don't have to 
worry about that until you get it to compile.

If this all seems to difficult, there *might* be someone who has a 
compiled version with this patch that he wants to post online.

